# Every text file checks out LF, on every OS and whatever core.autocrlf says. Tests read the tree
# as data: freshness gates byte-compare generated docs (decoder/hardware_matrix_test.go,
# decoder/capability_matrix_test.go, pull's embedded capability-matrix.json copy), cmd/gate
# round-trips testdata/gate_ledger.json and regex-reads scripts/refresh_parity_hashes.sh,
# examples/structured parses docs/use-from-go.md's code fences, and source-reading tests look for
# "\n}\n". A CRLF checkout (Windows' default autocrlf=true) broke all of those on the root-windows
# CI job, 2026-10-03. Every text file in the index was already LF, so this renormalizes nothing.
# Binary files are detected as before (text=auto) and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The first three pinned, before the rule above; kept explicit because their gates also strip CR
# (stripCR), and a Windows `-update` regeneration must write LF.
docs/hardware-matrix.md      text eol=lf
docs/capability-matrix.md    text eol=lf
docs/capability-matrix.json  text eol=lf
